course: dictionary
lesson: 5290
title: June: a month and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one. «The rhyme: "Thirty days hath September, April, June and November."» Here June sits in a list of months, so it is the sixth month of the year, between May and July.
explain: Now look at «June» in a sentence about a person: "June came to my party." Nobody has a party in a month, so June must be a girl's name. Capital letters help too, but the clues around the word are what really tell you.
explain: Always ask: what would fit here? Try "in June" or "June is" and see if it makes sense. «Grasses do not bother with any of that: they throw millions of tiny pollen grains into the wind, which is why so many people sneeze with hay fever in June.» Here June is a time of year, so it is a month.
fact: June is the sixth month of the year, between May and July.
fact: June has 30 days.
fact: June is also a girl's name.
fact: Phrases with June: «in June», «early June», «the end of June».
fact: In the northern half of the world (like the UK and USA), June is early summer with the longest days; in the southern half (like Australia), June is early winter with the shortest days.
exercise: Which month has 30 days, according to the rhyme «Thirty days hath September, April, June and November»? | 31 | *30 | 29 | 28
exercise: «Grasses throw millions of tiny pollen grains into the wind, which is why so many people sneeze with hay fever in June.» In which month do many people sneeze with hay fever? | December | Normandy | Thirty | *June
exercise: "June came to my party." Is June a month or a name here? | A month | A type of flower | *A girl's name | A day of the week
test: «On 21 June, la Fête de la musique, anyone can play music outside for free.» On which date is la Fête de la musique held? | 6 June | 1 May | *21 June | 30 June
test: In the northern half of the world, which is true about June? | It is early winter with the shortest days | It comes before May | It has 31 days | *It is early summer with the longest days
exam: Which month comes between May and July, and has 30 days? | September | April | *June | August
